        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(plugin-sdk): guard ingress effects once per event",
        "body": "Related: #109657\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nNon-idempotent command side effects can re-execute when a durable ingress row replays in the crash window between the side effect and its completion tombstone. This is part of the accepted fleet-wide at-least-once semantics from the durable-ingress program in #109657. Channels need an opt-in exactly-once-per-event guard for these effects.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a narrow Plugin SDK seam over the existing persistent-dedupe claim, commit, and release machinery, with no new storage. It propagates persistent-state failures fail-closed and documents the residual crash window honestly. qqbot adoption follows separately.\n\nAI-assisted implementation; maintainer-reviewed.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible impact until channels adopt the seam. Channel plugins can opt in to guard non-idempotent command effects against durable ingress replays.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Post-rebase focused Vitest: src/plugin-sdk/ingress-effect-once.test.ts, 11 of 11 passing, including transient commit recovery and normalized-prefix collision regressions.\n- Plugin SDK API baseline check: passing.\n- Plugin SDK export-sync check: passing.\n- Plugin SDK surface check: passing.\n- oxfmt on all touched files: passing with no diff.\n- Fresh final branch autoreview against origin/main: zero accepted or actionable findings.\n- Accepted Blacksmith Testbox Knip proof: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29652144372\n- Orchestrator review: claim, run, commit, and release semantics passed; persistent-dedupe disk-error propagation verified; residual at-least-once window accepted and documented.\n",
